{
  "id": 74,
  "title": "N-bit Adder/Subtractor",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "digital",
  "tags": [
    "arithmetic",
    "parameters",
    "combinational"
  ],
  "top": "add_sub",
  "synthesis": "required",
  "max_flip_flops": 0,
  "synth_params": {
    "N": 12
  },
  "languages": [
    "verilog",
    "systemverilog",
    "vhdl"
  ],
  "ports": [
    {
      "name": "a",
      "dir": "input",
      "width": 12
    },
    {
      "name": "b",
      "dir": "input",
      "width": 12
    },
    {
      "name": "sub",
      "dir": "input",
      "width": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "y",
      "dir": "output",
      "width": 12
    },
    {
      "name": "cout",
      "dir": "output",
      "width": 1
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "Parameter `N` (default 8). The judge uses **N = 12**.",
    "`sub = 0`: `{cout, y} = a + b`. `sub = 1`: `{cout, y} = a + ~b + 1`, i.e. `y = a − b`, with `cout = 1` when there is no borrow (`a ≥ b`).",
    "Use **one adder** for both operations: invert `b` with XOR gates and feed `sub` in as the carry-in. A reviewer would reject two separate adders plus a mux.",
    "Purely combinational."
  ],
  "hints": [
    "`b ^ {N{sub}}` conditionally inverts every bit of b.",
    "`{cout, y} = a + (b ^ {N{sub}}) + sub` in N+1 bits.",
    "In VHDL, `(N-1 downto 0 => sub)` builds the replicated vector."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "check": "add",
      "title": "add with carry",
      "input": "N=12, a = 12'hFFF, b = 12'h001, sub = 0",
      "expected": "y = 12'h000, cout = 1"
    },
    {
      "check": "subtract",
      "title": "no borrow",
      "input": "a = 12'h100, b = 12'h001, sub = 1",
      "expected": "y = 12'h0FF, cout = 1"
    },
    {
      "check": "subtract",
      "title": "borrow",
      "input": "a = 12'h000, b = 12'h001, sub = 1",
      "expected": "y = 12'hFFF, cout = 0"
    }
  ]
}
